      'a monotype is a one of a kind print you paint or draw an image in ink or paint on a smooth featureless surface a sheet of glass plexiglass or metal that has no permanent marks then lay paper on it and take one impression usually only one strong print is possible plus a faint ghost so it is called the painterly print no two can ever be alike',
      'a monoprint has a fixed repeatable matrix element an etched or engraved plate a woodblock a stencil that carries a base image which can be reprinted but each impression is then varied uniquely by hand inking a la poupee wiping adding a monotype layer or extra colour so each one is unique within a related series',
      'the short rule monotype has no matrix and cannot be repeated monoprint has a matrix but every pull is deliberately different',
